@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain

box Logic LOGIC_COLOR_T1
participant ":LogicManager" as Logic LOGIC_COLOR
participant ":ExportCommand" as Command LOGIC_COLOR
end box
box Model MODEL_COLOR_T1
participant "m:Model" as Model MODEL_COLOR
end box
box Storage STORAGE_COLOR_T1
participant "<<class>>\nCsvAddressBookExporter" as Exporter STORAGE_COLOR
end box
box Commons #FFFDF8
participant "<<class>>\nFileUtil" as FileUtil
end box

note over Logic, Command: Parsing has produced an ExportCommand; this trace shows a successful export.
[-> Logic : execute("export members.csv")
activate Logic
Logic -> Command : execute(m, rosterPath, preferencesPath)
activate Command
Command -> Model : getFilteredPersonList()
activate Model
Model --> Command : displayed members in displayed order
deactivate Model
Command -> Model : getAddressBook()
activate Model
Model --> Command : roster (for total member count)
deactivate Model
Command -> Command : snapshot displayed members and count hidden members
Command -> Command : resolve target path and check protected destinations
activate Command
Command --> Command
deactivate Command
note over Command
Invalid paths and protected files fail before writing.
Protected files include the active roster, preferences,
backup/recovery files, running JAR, and session lock.
end note
Command -> Exporter : export(people, targetPath)
activate Exporter
Exporter -> FileUtil : writeAtomically(filePath, writer)
activate FileUtil
FileUtil -> FileUtil : create sibling temporary file
activate FileUtil
FileUtil --> FileUtil
deactivate FileUtil
FileUtil -> Exporter : writer callback: writeCsv(people, temporary)
activate Exporter
note right of Exporter
The callback writes a UTF-8 header and
displayed members in displayed order using Commons CSV.
It closes the writer before returning.
end note
Exporter --> FileUtil
deactivate Exporter
FileUtil -> FileUtil : replace destination atomically
activate FileUtil
FileUtil --> FileUtil
deactivate FileUtil
note over Exporter, FileUtil
If writing or replacement throws, attempt temporary-file cleanup
and propagate the exception. The previous destination is preserved.
end note
FileUtil --> Exporter
deactivate FileUtil
Exporter --> Command
deactivate Exporter
Command --> Logic : CommandResult(exported count, path, and hidden count if any)
deactivate Command
Logic -> Command : isReadOnly()
activate Command
Command --> Logic : true
deactivate Command
[<-- Logic : CommandResult (no automatic JSON save)
deactivate Logic
note over Logic, Model: Export leaves the roster, filters, and sorting unchanged.
@enduml
